    verification: "Field verification: inspect the actual source and receptor; confirm controls are installed, suitable, maintained and used; compare monitoring only with applicable approved criteria; check instrument suitability/calibration and competent operator where measurements apply; document date, time, location, operating state, method, weather/context and result. Verify document revision, signatures, attachments, approvals, transfer destination/receipt where applicable, action closure and effectiveness. Escalate missing evidence or nonconformity; retain under approved retention schedule.",
    commonErrors: "Common errors: treating generic guidance as a legal limit; failing to identify receptors or cumulative impacts; starting before approvals/briefing; monitoring at an unrepresentative time/location; not recording operational context; mixing incompatible waste or using an unverified destination where waste topic applies; leaving failed controls in service; closing complaints/CAPA without effectiveness evidence; and not reassessing after change.",
    fieldExample: "Field example: For a planned activity involving trend analysis; recurring sources; control effectiveness; change management; continual improvement, the supervisor and Environmental Officer review site conditions and approved requirements, brief the crew, check controls and assign monitoring/inspection. If a complaint, abnormal reading, spill, rejected load or control defect occurs, they protect people/environment, notify the designated lead, record facts, correct the source, confirm effectiveness and retain evidence before close-out.",
    checklist: "Pre-start checklist: definition/scope understood; aspects and receptors identified; UAE/emirate/permit obligations verified; approvals and method statement current; hierarchy of controls applied; owner and competent persons assigned; crew/contractors briefed; equipment/containment inspected; monitoring and trigger response ready where applicable; emergency/complaint route known; documents and attachments controlled; deviation/CAPA closed with effectiveness check.",
    interview: "Interview preparation: Explain the topic in your own words; purpose and applicability; source-pathway-receptor; relevant UAE federal and emirate/permit verification process; aspects/impacts and risk/significance method; hierarchy of controls; technical parameters and why numeric values must come from applicable official approval; monitoring/inspection frequency basis; competency and document roles; stop-work/emergency response; site example; common failure and corrective action. For any number, state its source, jurisdiction, revision and applicability rather than guessing.",
  ),
];
